"map <ESC> <ESC>:noh<CR>
noremap <ESC> :noh<CR><ESC>
nnoremap <Esc><Esc> :let @/ = ""<CR>
set autoindent
set smartindent
set gdefault
set history=2000
set hlsearch
set ignorecase
set incsearch
set keymodel=startsel
set noexpandtab
set nowrap
set scrolloff=3
set selection=inclusive
set shiftwidth=4
set showcmd
set smartcase
set softtabstop=4
set tabstop=4
set timeout
set ttimeout
set timeoutlen=0
set ttimeoutlen=0
"set clipboard=unnamed
"Using the unnamed clipboard causes VsVim to freeze Visual Studio, but the following mappings purport to fix that (they don't)
"noremap y "*y
"noremap yy "*yy
"noremap Y "*y$
"noremap d "*d
"noremap dd "*dd
"noremap D "*D
"noremap p "*p
"noremap P "*P
"" black hole register for x because chars do not need to go in any accessible register anyway
"noremap x "_x
" BUT THIS - THIS FINALLY GETS IT TO WORK THE WAY I WANT IT TO WITHOUT STALLING THE EDITOR: (Modified from something found at https://github.com/VsVim/VsVim/issues/3116#issuecomment-2377659591)
vnoremap y :vsc edit.copy<CR>gv"0y
noremap yy :vsc edit.copy<CR>"0yy
